    <h4>Why are Ocean+ Data Viewer and Ocean+ Library being retired?</h4>

    <p>Ocean+ Data Viewer and Ocean+ Library have long been trusted sources of marine data. However, the development of
      newer platforms with superior functionality, usability, and data curation means that there are now better alternatives
      for accessing marine data.</p>
    <p>Retiring Ocean+ Data Viewer and Ocean+ Library will enable us to focus on the most impactful areas of Ocean+, like <a
        target="_blank" href="https://habitats.oceanplus.org/">Ocean+ Habitats</a>. It will also allow us to direct users to more up-to-date
      platforms that are better able to meet their needs, like <a target="_blank" href="https://unbiodiversitylab.org/en/">UN Biodiversity
        Lab</a>, <a target="_blank" href="https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/home/index.html">UNEP-WCMC GIS Portal</a>, and the <a
        target="_blank" href="https://www.proteuspartners.org/">Proteus website</a> for members of the <a
        target="_blank" href="https://www.proteuspartners.org/">Proteus Partnership</a>.</p>
    <p>With the exception of a small number of datasets that have been superseded by newer datasets (please see
      <b>Which Ocean+ Data Viewer datasets will no longer be available?</b> below),
      all of the marine datasets on Ocean+ Data Viewer and Ocean+ Library
      will still be available through these alternative platforms.</p>
    <p>To share any questions or concerns you may have about this transition, please respond to the surveys available on the
      Ocean+ Data Viewer and Ocean+ Library websites.</p>
    <h4>When will Ocean+ Data Viewer and Ocean+ Library be retired?</h4>
    <p>Both will be retired in early 2025.</p>
    <h4>Where can I find the information that was hosted on Ocean+ Library?</h4>
    <p>A full copy of the Ocean+ Library database will now be available to download on the <a
        target="_blank" href="https://resources.unep-wcmc.org/products/WCMC_DT007">UNEP-WCMC Resources</a> page.</p>

    <h4>Where can I find or view the datasets that were hosted on Ocean+ Data Viewer?</h4>

    <p>Ocean+ Data Viewer's datasets are now openly available through the <a
        target="_blank" href="https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/home/gallery.html?view=grid&amp;sortOrder=desc&amp;sortField=relevance&amp;tags=ocean%2B">Ocean+
        tag on UNEP-WCMC GIS Portal</a>. This is our recommended platform for users who wish to download the data, view
      single map layers (members of the <a target="_blank" href="https://www.proteuspartners.org/">Proteus Partnership</a> can view multiple
      map layers when logged in), or who already have GIS expertise.</p>
    <p>Otherwise, if you are not a Proteus Partnership member but still wish to view multiple data layers on a map, many of
      Ocean+ Data Viewer's datasets will be openly available to view (with enhanced usability) on <a
        target="_blank" href="https://map.unbiodiversitylab.org/">UN Biodiversity Lab</a>. Apart from these Ocean+ datasets, <a
        target="_blank" href="https://map.unbiodiversitylab.org/">UN Biodiversity Lab</a> also contains a large variety of other marine and
      terrestrial maps and is regularly updated with the most recent quality data.</p>
