    <h4>Which Ocean+ Data Viewer datasets will no longer be available?</h4>

    <p>As part of the transition to <a target="_blank" href="https://unbiodiversitylab.org/en/">UN Biodiversity Lab</a> and <a
        target="_blank" href="https://data-gis.unep-wcmc.org/portal/home/index.html">UNEP-WCMC GIS Portal</a>, a small minority of datasets
      will be retired and not available on either platform. These are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>Mean Annual Sea Surface Chlorophyll-a Concentration (2009-2013)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Mean Annual Sea Surface Temperature (2003-2007)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Mean Annual Sea Surface Temperature (2009-2013)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Mean Sea Surface Productivity in December (2003-2007)</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Mean Sea Surface Productivity in June (2003-2007)</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>In each case these have been superseded by newer datasets that contain other advantages, like greater temporal
      coverage. These alternatives can be found at:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>Chlorophyll-a: <a
            target="_blank" href="https://map.unbiodiversitylab.org/earth?basemap=grayscale&amp;coordinates=20,0,2&amp;layers=chlorophyll-a-concentration-in-seawater-1998-2023_100">Chlorophyll-a
            concentration in seawater 1998-2023</a> on UN Biodiversity Lab</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Sea surface temperature: <a target="_blank" href="https://neo.gsfc.nasa.gov/view.php?datasetId=MYD28M">Sea Surface Temperature
            (MODIS, 2002+)</a> at Nasa Earth Observations</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>Sea surface productivity: <a href="http://orca.science.oregonstate.edu/npp_products.php">NPP Products</a> on the
          Oregon State University Ocean Productivity website</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Will all datasets have the same use restrictions and licenses as when they were hosted on Ocean+ Data Viewer?</h4>

    <p>Yes, nothing has changed with respect to use and licensing. For all licensing enquiries, please contact <a
        href="mailto:oceanplus@unep-wcmc.org">oceanplus@unep-wcmc.org</a>.</p>

    <h4>Will the retirement of Ocean+ Data Viewer and Ocean+ Library have any effect on Ocean+ Habitats?</h4>

    <p>No, Ocean+ Habitats is not affected by these changes.</p>
